  "Question": "The center of a triangle's incircle (the incenter) is",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "The intersection of the perpendicular bisectors of the three sides",
    "B": "The intersection of the three angle bisectors",
    "C": "The intersection of the three altitudes"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The center of the incircle is equidistant from the three sides, so it lies on the bisectors of the three interior angles and is their point of intersection.",
